Source:     https://github.com/DEShawResearch/random123
Version:    1.14.0
Revision:   9545ff6 (upstream main, five commits after the v1.14.0 tag)

The Version field above is the pinned upstream release, and it is the only
`Version:` line in this file on purpose: .github/workflows/vendor-upstream.yml
reads it with `sed -n 's/^Version: *//p'` to ask whether upstream has shipped
a newer release. Keep it in step when re-vendoring.

Provides the counter-based generators behind every sampler in this package:
Philox4x64-10 (the default engine) and Threefry4x64-13. Reference: J. K. Salmon, M. A. Moraes,
R. O. Dror and D. E. Shaw (2011), "Parallel random numbers: as easy as
1, 2, 3", SC '11, <doi:10.1145/2063384.2063405>.


